{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-246855",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225277/assets/7e7ddf9e0a6edbfd5521ca5de1d718ab9c66b7e0a96ed8d52798fd16daf63aa5.png)\n\nThe reference angle, denoted ${\\theta }_{R},$  is the angle that $\\theta ={200}^{∘}$ makes with the $x$-axis.\n\nAs $\\theta $ is in the third quadrant, its reference angle is given by\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}=\\theta -{180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}={200}^{∘}-{180}^{∘}={20}^{∘}.\n$$",
